@testray.main.component.name = "Patcher Builder"

Feature: Patcher Builder and 71 builds
	Testing creation of 71 builds on Patcher Builder.

Setup:
	* I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage

Scenario: Run fix pack builder hotfix 7x job
	As a TSE, I should be able to run the fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x job

	Given I start the fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x job for the "next" branch with the following parameters
	| fix.pack.customer.ticket         | LRGROW-72                                                                                     |
	| fix.pack.built.for               | LRGROW                                                                                        |
	| fix.pack.fixed.issues            | LPE-0                                                                                         |
	| fix.pack.hotfixed.issues         | GROW-110,GROW-13,GROW-446,GROW-498,GROW-508,LPS-113730,LPS-113733,LPS-79691,LPS-83386,OWXP-91 |
	| fix.pack.id                      | 170538318                                                                                     |
	| git.revision                     | eb1801be18eb95961c65089e2b8d15c23b5fb1c0                                                      |
	| patcher.build.id                 | 170538727                                                                                     |
	| patcher.user.id                  | 01234                                                                                         |
	| patcher.fix.delivery.method      | Fix Pack 3.0                                                                                  |
	| release.tool.git.remote.username | eszterdudasschveder                                                                           |
	| release.tool.git.branch          | fpf4-1-168556409                                                                              |
	| fix.pack.baseCommittish          | fix-pack-dxp-6-7110                                                                           |
	| patcher.security.patch           | false                                                                                         |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I get the current build number for the job titled "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat-test)"
	And I check the job with the name "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	Then the job with the name "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful

Scenario: Run test fix pack builder install job
	As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-install job

	Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-install job for the "next" branch with the following parameters
	| bundle       | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/portal/7.1.10/liferay-dxp-tomcat-7.1.10-ga1-20180703090613030.zip                                            |
	| fixPack      | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/7.1.10/dxp/liferay-fix-pack-dxp-3-7110.zip                                                         |
	| hotfix       | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.1.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-012-7110.zip  |
	| patchingTool | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-172.16.168/ee/fix-packs/patching-tool/patching-tool-2.0.8.zip                                                              |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-install(uat-test)"
	And I wait for "4" minutes
	And I stop the job titled "test-fixpack-builder-install(uat-test)"
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-install(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
	Then the test-fixpack-builder-install console log should not have any visible errors

Scenario: Run test fix pack builder patch difference job
	As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference job

	Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference job for the "next" branch with the following parameters
	| alphaPath | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder-backup/fix-packs/7.1.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-234-7110-alpha.zip |
	| betaPath  | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.1.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-234-7110.zip              |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(uat-test)"
	And I check the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	Then the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful
	When I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I go to the console output for the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}"
	Then the test-fixpack-builder-patch-difference console log should not have any visible errors

Scenario: Save current hotfix
	As a TSE, I should be able to run the test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy job

	Given I start the test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy job for the "next" branch with the following parameters
	| destinationFilePath | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder-backup/fix-packs/7.1.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-234-7110-alpha.zip |
	| originFilePath      | /mnt/mfs-hdd1-10.50.0.33/live/opt/java/jenkins/userContent/liferay-fix-pack-builder/fix-packs/7.1.10/hotfix/liferay-hotfix-234-7110.zip              |
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	And I get the current build number for the short job titled "test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy(uat-test)"
	And I check the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" for completion
	And I go to the Patcher Builder Jenkins homepage
	Then the job with the name "test-fixpack-builder-hotfix-copy(uat-test)" and build number "${staticJobBuildNumber}" should have been successful